    <div class="references">
      <p>Bateson, M.C. (2010). <span class="italic">Composing a further life: The age of active wisdom.</span> New York, NY: Knopf.</p>
      <p>Cohen, G. D. (2005). <span class="italic">The mature mind: The positive power of the aging brain.</span> New York, NY: Basic Books.</p>
      <p>Edmondson, R. (2015). <span class="italic">Ageing, insight and wisdom: Meaning and practice across the lifecourse.</span> Bristol, UK: Policy Press.</p>
      <p>Erikson, E.H. &amp; Erikson, J.M. (1998). <span class="italic">The life cycle completed: Extended version.</span> New York, NY: W. W. Norton.</p>
      <p>Hodgkin, S. (2012). &lsquo;I&rsquo;m older and more interested in my community&rsquo;: Older people&rsquo;s contributions to social capital. <span class="italic">Australasian Journal on Ageing, 31</span>(1), 34-39. doi:10.1111/j.1741-6612.2011.00538.x</p>
      <p>Keisari S. &amp; Palgi, Y. (2017). Life-crossroads on stage: Integrating life review and drama therapy for older adults. <span class="italic">Aging and Mental Health, Volume 21, Issue 10, 1079-1089.</span></p>
      <p>Pevny, R. (2014). Conscious aging: embrace and savour your next chapter. Simon &amp; Schuster Inc.; New York, New York.</p>
      <p>McAdams D &amp; de St Aubin, E. (1992). A theory of generativity and its assessment through self-report, behavioral acts, and narrative themes in autobiography. <span class="italic">Journal of Personality and Social Psychology: 50</span> (1240&ndash;1252).</p>
      <p>Rowe, J. &amp; Kahn, R. (1998). Successful aging. New York, NY: Dell.</p>
      <p>Tornstam, L. (2005). <span class="italic">Gerotranscendence: A developmental theory of positive aging.</span> New York, NY: Springer Publishing Company.</p>
      <p>Wengraf, T. (2004). Qualitative research Interviewing: Biographic narrative and semi-structured methods. Thousand Oaks, California: SAGE Publications Ltd.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

